oodreads.com/review/list/27036454?shelf=book-box"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"ebook","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/27036454?shelf=ebook"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2505053406"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TezkqQulWcExnWE61IFuCQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TezkqQulWcExnWE61IFuCQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:27036454"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1780679576000,"createdAt":1578590431886,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1653964448255,"text":"\u003cb\u003eTHIS WAS SO BLOODY GOOD. HOW AM I MEANT TO WAIT A YEAR FOR THE NEXT ONE?!?!!!\u003c/b\u003e 😭😩\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1613705439ra/30891640.gif\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eRight. So, I'll be brief as to not \u003ci\u003espoil\u003c/i\u003e anyone. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI know \u003cb\u003eLara\u003c/b\u003e made some pretty \u003ci\u003emajor mistakes\u003c/i\u003e in the previous instalment, but I thought that she was treated a bit \u003cb\u003eunfairly\u003c/b\u003e here, despite her vigorous efforts to make up for all of her wrongdoings. I absolutely \u003ci\u003eLOVED\u003c/i\u003e meeting all of her sisters though and seeing how protective they were of each other. 💙 I also really want to see them bond with their brother, Keris, in the future books!\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eAren\u003c/b\u003e, especially, \u003ci\u003efrustrated\u003c/i\u003e me because he was so flip-floppy. He was a man who was so used to having his country \u003ci\u003eAND\u003c/i\u003e his queen, that when faced with \u003ci\u003ehaving to choose\u003c/i\u003e between the two...he turned into an \u003cb\u003eindecisive idiot\u003c/b\u003e. I just wish that there'd have been a more satisfactory reunion for the two of them at the end of the book. It was a tad \u003ci\u003eanticlimactic\u003c/i\u003e. That's literally the \u003ci\u003eonly criticism\u003c/i\u003e that I have. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBut not to worry! There were some definite swoon-worthy parts that had me \u003cb\u003eaudibly squealing\u003c/b\u003e in happiness, despite the wee hours in the morning. I read this whole thing in two sittings, refusing to put it down until it was finished at 5am because \u003ci\u003eYES\u003c/i\u003e...it was \u003ci\u003eTHAT GOOD\u003c/i\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI genuinely \u003cb\u003ecan't wait\u003c/b\u003e for the next two books in the series, even though it follows two new characters, who were introduced in this instalment. Watch me re-read \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/43383182.The_Bridge_Kingdom__The_Bridge_Kingdom___1_\" title=\"The Bridge Kingdom (The Bridge Kingdom, #1) by Danielle L. Jensen\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eThe Bridge Kingdom\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/51887283.The_Traitor_Queen__The_Bridge_Kingdom___2_\" title=\"The Traitor Queen (The Bridge Kingdom, #2) by Danielle L. Jensen\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eThe Traitor Queen\u003c/a\u003e \u003cb\u003e*again*\u003c/b\u003e before the end of the year, haha. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI \u003ci\u003eHIGHLY\u003c/i\u003e recommend picking this series up, if you haven't yet. It's Danielle L. Jensen's best series to date...and that's saying something! ;)","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2POEH0IL77EZ8\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.3rgsN5x56wkEadM8\"}}"},"likeCount":496,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":50},"User:127632948":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":127632948,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1729856926i/127632948._UX200_CR0,25,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":3523,"textReviewsCount":909,"name":"Clace ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/127632948-clace","contributor":null,"id":127632948},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.9ZiFK0gBLtvdUPoa":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.9ZiFK0gBLtvdUPoa"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.9ZiFK0gBLtvdUPoa\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.9ZiFK0gBLtvdUPoa","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.9ZiFK0gBLtvdUPoa"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/127632948?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7788415281"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TiVnvZEKt7iu6ijqr0785w":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TiVnvZEKt7iu6ijqr0785w","creator":{"__ref":"User:127632948"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785555922683,"createdAt":1753982843900,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1755469387342,"text":"\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e5 stars!!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e“Awake or asleep, all I see is your face. All I hear is your voice. All I feel is you in my arms. All I want is you.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhere do I even start with this book? This book was a rollercoaster of emotions. No one does it like Danielle L. Jensen. It's the fact that this book can stand out without the romance that impresses me because so few books can achieve that. What I loved the most about this book was how unpredictable it was like till the last minute I had no idea how things were going to be resolved, like I was so fucking stressed because how were they going to resolve everything but Danielle just managed to do that and Idk how her brain works but it was done so swiftly + it was so stunning, the whole process, the chapters ALL OF THEM ended with cliffhangers and the stakes were extremely high, I was so engrossed in this book that I honestly did not care for anything else. The chapters were also small, so that just made this book even better, but to not only match the hype as its predecessor but to surpass it was amazing.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“But in his heart, he knew that even if he never saw her again for the rest of his life, it would never be over.\u003cbr /\u003eShe would always be his queen.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eLara\u003c/b\u003e, the patience that she had!! I loved it. The way her mind works is so amazing to me, the way she crafts her plans and how she's so ruthless with them, and I also loved seeing her side with her siblings, it was so good!! Like the small glimpses of Keris and the 12 (?) sisters reminded me a bit of 12 dancing princess but I loveeed all of them especially sahrina and how she put a dagger at Arens throat 🙂‍↕️ I love, love, love how determined she was to get her out and the way she achieved that 😭😭 had me breathless that entire sequence was so well written that i forgot how to breathe. What I loved the most about her was how much she cared for Aren and Ithicana, if that was a side of her that I loved to see. \u003cb\u003eAren\u003c/b\u003e, I love him and his anger was 100% justified but I got a bit of peace when he would call out Lara and get clocked instead 😭 the way he was able to move past all of that and still trust her and believe in her was so good of him, his love for his people put me at the edge of my seat because he was split whether to choose his people or Lara and that had me in a state where I wanted to scream in a pillow until someone told me how it would be resolved, I did not see the resolution coming but I did like it.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“You are my goddamned damnation, but there will never be anyone but you.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe \u003cb\u003eromance\u003c/b\u003e, was sooo good, what amazes me is how she can write a gut wrenching romance that has you engrossed in it despite the character getting together in the first book but the circumstances that she puts the characters under create so much yearning and angst that you just fall more in love it and crave for more and more, the tension that these two characters had was off the charts and their chemistry was dripping down the pages, the betrayal just heightened all of that up, the moments put against them are used so well to make the romance and shine and tow eave the plot through that honestly spectacular, it was also kind of a slow burn and the spice did not disappoint the yearning and the wait, honestly I had zero complaints. Also, the scenes of them wanting each other but distancing themselves for the sake of their people had me SCREAMINGGGGG.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“She was everything. Mind, body, and soul, she was everything he wanted. Everything he needed. The queen Ithicana needed.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe plot and the world building\u003c/b\u003e, the plot was fully fleshed out, with high stakes and unpredictable plot twists, everything turned out to be amazing. The best part was not knowing what was going to happen next everything that was happening made the whole atmosphere so tense and I honestly loved that whole experience, I liked that this book focused more on Madriana and its land, I also liked Lara and Aren exploring the area Lara and her sisters were trained, the distinguishing difference between Ithicana and Madriana is so well done and also loved to see Zarrah's land (I forgot the name) but I cant wait for Danielle to venture off their. The way her politics are scattered across this aspect is also something I look forward to.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOverall, I loved it and I can't wait to read the next two books!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“Forgive her. She loves you.\"\u003cbr /\u003eHe dropped the old woman's arm, feeling Lara's gaze on him. Knowing she was listening. \"she doesn't know what love is.\"\u003cbr /\u003e\"That's why you should forgive her.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e__\u003cbr /\u003eJaw on the floor, heart in pieces ALSO on the floor, body on the floor sobbing 😔✋🏻\u003cbr /\u003e___\u003cbr /\u003eMy jaw is still on the floor with the way book 1 ended. I can't wait for the yearning, betrayals, and spice 🙂‍↕️\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBuddy reading with \u003cb\u003eHoda\u003c/b\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.9ZiFK0gBLtvdUPoa\"}}"},"likeCount":324,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":79},"User:161765044":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":161765044,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1779337060i/161765044._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":720,"textReviewsCount":72,"name":"jasmine •｡ꪆৎ ˚⋅","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/161765044-jasmine","contributor":null,"id":161765044},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.ADb8gezEL7SuqGme\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodr