😭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLara and Aren absolutely shredded my soul. Lara stays THAT GIRL exiled, betrayed, hated and still out here proving herself like the queen she is. And Aren?? My emotionally tortured king, constantly torn between the woman he loves and the people he swore to protect. And you know what? He was so valid though… \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ethis was so much better than the first one! faster paced, more action, more tension, and the ANGST??? Immaculate. The heartbreak?? The political mess?? The action?? Perfection. This book had me stressed, feral, and obsessed from start to finish. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ealso I’m kinda hesitant to continue this series because i found out the rest of the books isn’t even in their POV anymore??? Like, why would you do this to me I’m not ready to let them go yet 🥲","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A23B6ZYC298QAS\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.ADb8gezEL7SuqGme\"}}"},"likeCount":64,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:160690374":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":160690374,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1769880772i/160690374._UY200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":158,"textReviewsCount":142,"name":"giuliana","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/160690374-giuliana","contributor":null,"id":160690374},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1NOVLYNEPHT81":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1NOVLYNEPHT81"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1NOVLYNEPHT81\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1NOVLYNEPHT81","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1NOVLYNEPHT81"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/160690374?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"2023-books","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/160690374?shelf=2023-books"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5741363610"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.8u1hsoANih8cjw8lNvJp0A":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.8u1hsoANih8cjw8lNvJp0A","creator":{"__ref":"User:160690374"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1742990368594,"createdAt":1692573219146,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1692635282127,"text":"4⭐️\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e⚠️\u003cu\u003eTHIS REVIEW CONTAINS SPOILERS\u003c/u\u003e⚠️\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/50719471.The_Traitor_Queen__The_Bridge_Kingdom___2_\" title=\"The Traitor Queen (The Bridge Kingdom, #2) by Danielle L. Jensen\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eThe Traitor Queen\u003c/a\u003e by \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/author/show/7091823.Danielle_L__Jensen\" title=\"Danielle L. Jensen\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eDanielle L. Jensen\u003c/a\u003e is a YA fantasy romance book and the second of the series called \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/53921926.The_Bridge_Kingdom__The_Bridge_Kingdom___1_\" title=\"The Bridge Kingdom (The Bridge Kingdom, #1) by Danielle L. Jensen\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eThe Bridge Kingdom\u003c/a\u003e, which are separate duologies and can be read individually.\u003cbr\u003eA queen now in exile as a traitor, Lara has watched Ithicana be conquered by her own father, helpless to do anything to stop the destruction. But when she learns her husband, Aren, has been captured in battle, Lara knows there is only one reason her father is keeping him alive: as bait for his traitorous daughter. And it is bait she fully intends to take.\u003cbr\u003eRisking her life to the Tempest Seas, Lara returns to Ithicana with a plan not only to free its king, but for liberating the Bridge Kingdom from her father’s clutches using his own weapons: the sisters whose lives she spared. But not only is the palace inescapable, there are more players in the game than Lara ever realized, enemies and allies switching sides in the fight for crowns, kingdoms, and bridges. But her greatest adversary of all might be the very man she’s trying to free – the husband she betrayed.\u003cbr\u003eWith everything she loves in jeopardy, Lara must decide who - and what – she is fighting for: her kingdom, her husband, or herself.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e➵Kings and queens make decisions, but it is the common folk who pay the price.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1692573560i/34629670._SY540_.png\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" alt=\"the traitor queen aesthetic\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e➵Just because a choice is hard doesn’t mean you don’t make it.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cu\u003eThe characters\u003c/u\u003e:\u003cbr\u003eWhen I read the first book, I wanted so bad to know what \u003cb\u003eLara\u003c/b\u003e was capable of and although it was more like an insight of it, this book did not disappoint. I thought I couldn’t love her more than I already did but she’s just incredibly amazing, I LOVE reading about strong women getting revenge but this was crazy in a very good way. She’s not the same person after the events that occurred in The Bridge Kingdom, plagued by guilt and shame for her role in the deaths many Ithicanians and innocent people, she decides to do everything in her power to save her home, its people and of course her husband Aren. The fact that she didn’t let pain take over her just to save the people she loved was admirable, even getting through her fear of the sea to save her husband was just on point. From slitting throats to climbing and trying not to get bitten by snakes to almost die, she achieves her goal impeccably with blood, tears and pain. It was totally understandable the fact that everyone in Ithicana hated her, but she won their trust back flawlessly. What a woman, I am in awe. I love women written by women who are strong, powerful, not scared to show their feelings, beautiful inside and out, fighters, who don’t need men to save them and many more things. Lara will always be my favorite character in this series, period.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eAren\u003c/b\u003e has changed too, due to his wife’s betrayal and being captured by his enemy, Lara’s father. I really like his character and how much he loves his people, willing to do anything to save them. He’s fighting his feelings because he doesn’t want to still love Lara, but it is pretty clear he’ll always be in love with her and deep down he knows what she did was a mistake. Also, he’s too handsome to handle it \u003cs\u003e(and I would let him do anything to me)\u003c/s\u003e. I don’t think I have too much to say about him, just that he’s an incredible character and I’ll always say he’s an incredible king to his people.\u003cbr\u003eI adored \u003cb\u003eLara’s sisters\u003c/b\u003e and I can’t wait to know more about them. Also, I’m asking for a petition for the author to write a book about Bronwyn, thank you. \u003cbr\u003eAnd… \u003cb\u003eKeris and Zarrah\u003c/b\u003e: as soon as I buy the third book of the series I will read it immediately because I can’t wait for them to fall in love and read about their enemies to lovers story.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e➵There was something about her.\u003cbr\u003eSomething that had spoken to his soul in a way no other woman he'd met ever had.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cu\u003eMy opinion\u003c/u\u003e:\u003cbr\u003eThis book did not disappoint at all. First of all, I couldn’t put it down, it was impossible. Also, short chapters and fast-paced? Sign me in. I read it in English on my kindle because I couldn’t wait for it to be translated to Spanish and now I’ve decided I’ll buy the whole series in its original language (and also hardcover because they’re SO freaking beautiful). Every interaction between Aren and Lara made me feel so on edge, such tension should be illegal. This book is packed with action from beginning to end, and on top of that, there’s a lot of soul searching from Lara and Aren, both struggling with each other and that completely broke me because I swear there were times where I thought they weren’t going to end up together and it was pure pain. The author’s writing is really good and the worldbuilding was also great, I enjoyed this book more than the first one because the translation in Spanish wasn’t good and I couldn’t appreciate her writing correctly. Of course the enemies to lovers and second chance romance was perfect, and although there’s only one spicy scene, I loved it and felt it was enough. The tears, the lack of trust, the hope, the desperate cries for one another in battle even thought they aren’t supposed to care? I can’t explain everything that I felt while reading this, going from shouting and screaming to completely breaking my heart (I didn’t cry though, so everything’s good).\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf I have to say something \u003cu\u003ebad\u003c/u\u003e about it and why I didn’t give it 5 stars would be:\u003cbr\u003e1. I wished there were more Aren and Lara scenes.\u003cbr\u003e2. It was too fast, I loved it but also didn’t like it (if that even makes sense).\u003cbr\u003e3. There’s some characters that should’ve appeared more.\u003cbr\u003e4. The end was really abrupt and it would’ve been better if it ended with an epilogue/conclusion to know more about their future. I just hope in the next books there’s some scenes of them.\u003cbr\u003e5. The death of Lara’s father felt a little too easy for me after all the damage he caused.\u003cbr\u003e6. Sometimes all the political stuff was too much and it bored me a little.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e➵You are my goddamned damnation, but there will never be anyone but you.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you like and want to read a good enemies to lovers, with tension, a little of spice, “touch her and you die” tropes and strong main characters, this fantasy series is for you.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBut before reading, check the \u003cb\u003etrigger warnings\u003c/b\u003e as there may be some topics that can be hard for some people (\u003cu\u003etw such as\u003c/u\u003e: war, death, blood, graphic, violence, torture, captivity, poisoning, +18 content, injury detail, etc.).\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e➵She was everything. Mind, body, and soul, she was everything he wanted. Everything he needed. The queen Ithicana needed.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eLast but not least, to my beautiful \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/158309030-lyra-semi-hiatus-cardan-s-tail-s-version-cardan-s-version\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eLyra (Cardan's tail's version) (Cardan’s version)\u003c/a\u003e: thank you for buddy reading this with me my love! We both love these characters so much and the fact that we can scream and curse together because of them is the best part💖\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e➵Awake or asleep, all I see is your face. All I hear is your voice. All I feel is you in my arms. All I want is you.\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e----------------------------------\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eREVIEWS AND RATINGS OF THE SERIES (so far)\u003c/b\u003e:\u003cbr\u003e-1. \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5555365104\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eThe Bridge Kingdom\u003c/a\u003e: 4/5\u003cbr\u003e-2. *The Traitor Queen*: 4/5\u003cbr\u003e-3. The Inadequate Heir: -\u003cbr\u003e-3.5. The Calm Before The Storm (novella): -\u003cbr\u003e-4. The Endless War: to be released (5th October, 2023)\u003cbr\u003e-Books 5 \u0026amp; 6: ?\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e(English is not my first language, if you find any mistakes please let me know).","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1NOVLYNEPHT81\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t\"}}"},"likeCount":58,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":19},"User:22314328":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":22314328,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1554984281i/22314328._UY200_CR33,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":409,"textReviewsCount":405,"name":"Aoife - Bookish_Babbling","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/22314328-aoife---bookish-babbling","contributor":null,"id":22314328},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3BRS6QLZZGI78":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3BRS6QLZZGI78"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3BRS6QLZZGI78\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3BRS6QLZZGI78","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3BRS6QLZZGI78"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22314328?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"read-in-2021","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22314328?shelf=read-in-2021"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"rage-reads","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22314328?shelf=rage-reads"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"read-kindle","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22314328?shelf=read-kindle"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3833405418"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.m4x-y5QwUb6dzOPYcfXyOg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.m4x-y5QwUb6dzOPYcfXyOg","creator":{"__ref":"User:22314328"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1765618588682,"createdAt":1613293160376,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1613293840032,"text":"Positives\u003cbr /\u003eI preferred this to book1, the things I liked about the first instalment namely world \u0026amp; side characters were added to in this one, sadly just not nearly enough for this rating to be much higher 🤷‍♀️\u003cbr /\u003eI liked how the world expanded and the new characters that were introduced - but we did not get to spend nearly enough time with them (or Ahnna for that matter)! However the fact that the later books are rumoured to focus on some of these characters gives me hope and may entice me to pick them up. I cannot pretend I am not curious about the next pairing especially considering where this book left off altho I do hope we get some flashbacks to see how the strongly hinted at relationship began 😈 🤐\u003cbr /\u003eI'm also crossing my fingers and lowkey hoping for more page time for the amazing siblings that only got a small yet impactful cameo in this book. I'd really love to find out so much more about each of them - such interesting lives they could lead as mercenaries or just in general trying to pick up the pieces and/or putting their lives together despite what they've been put through. The stories and mental health representation that could be told through these PoV as each adjusts to a new normal while reckoning with their pasts could be fascinating novellas.\u003cbr /\u003eIf this route is chosen please don't pair them all off and have \"love\" (ab)solve everything that came before - soz if the cranky cynical spinster is showing 🙈\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOn to what I disliked - AREN\u003cbr /\u003e🤬🙄😡\u003cbr /\u003eI found him naive \u0026amp; irksome in book1. I couldn't see the amazing leader we were told he was and this just got worse for me in this book as he continued to make stupidly selfish decisions while being an absolute ass for a good 60% of the story \u0026amp; then doubled down with some more dumb decisions as the end neared...I just don't see how I'm supposed to like or root for him when almost every decision he made about his relationship seemed to be the wrong one and/or for dumb reasons! Or rather he'd make a seemingly right decision, but then fail to follow through \u0026amp; toss the cat amongst the pigeons with his actions *exasperated-sigh*\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe ending was rather ridiculous \u0026amp; pretty far fetched even for a fantasy read - if anyone else has read this please share thoughts in spoiler tags below because erm...whut?! 🙄🤦‍♀️\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLast thing that really got to me, was that this series is pitched as a sexy romance read?\u003cbr /\u003eHard NOPE to this I'm afraid.\u003cbr /\u003eThe sex scenes (one per book) were so misplaced imho! \u003cbr /\u003eJust NO!\u003cbr /\u003eI didn't particularly find them sexy as the timing of both were seriously WTF?! moments for me. \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"c0e0151d-9df6-464e-978c-eed7cfe23768\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"c0e0151d-9df6-464e-978c-eed7cfe23768\"\u003eBook1 Lara had almost drowned amongst many others revelations that rocked her sheltered/curated beliefs that day \u0026amp; book 2 her leg was practically hanging off?! Ok so it had been stitched, but seriously...blood loss people?!\u003cbr /\u003eNot to mention the mental impact of the lead up to both scenarios - i just don't get it \u0026amp; then he walks out. WHAT THE ACTUAL FUCK - you absolute moronic coward! I didn't love Lara in book1, but she deserves so much better than what he's been shown capable of offering her in terms of emotional support as she's going to have so much to unpack when the dust settles - cockroach or no \u0026amp; there's no doubting she's a survivor...i just don't like him for her 😯\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAm I alone here on this ledge of wth kind of timing was that for these scenes?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eTo finish on a more positive note Lara was much improved for me in this. Altho tbf, prob not hard considering so many of her choices were maddening in the first book. Sure the ending was kind of Mary Sue levels of ridic but I enjoyed her character arc and growth through the earlier parts of the story + seeing how she went about atoning for the consequences of her decisions \u0026amp; (in)actions in the previous instalment. The bad ass we were told about in the first book came to play, she had many action filled scenes to show off the training we were told about and her scheming + plotting was more interesting to read about than the vaguely boring poisoning and sneaking about activities of the earlier book. Plus she was willing to make the sacrifices that Aren kept foiling with his wishy washy back and forth inability to stick to his decisions *sigh*\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOops this was supposed to be ending on a positive note so prob best I not linger on the character that deffo irked me the most over both books but especially this one. Cannot say I'm not lowkey glad the rest of the series will follow other characters while I wait to see if I'll continue with it...guess it depends on price of kindle versions and/or whether my library gets copies 😅\u003cbr /\u003eI am curious to see how the next MCs handle the fall out from the ending of this book as it'll deffo move up their timeline \u0026amp; I'm wondering how this pairing will even work considering the Romeo + Juliet \"our families are mortal enemies\" type set up 🤔\u003cbr /\u003eI really hope wherever this series goes that the scheming long game MC we met in this book and the rule bending general don't become wishy washy love lost puppies that make silly decisions risking their kingdoms *ahem* \u0026amp; that the cameo scene stealing siblings make welcome returns somehow 😇\u003cbr /\u003eAlthough I'm not holding my breath on that front as sadly I think they may be fridged 😕 \u003cbr /\u003eIn saying that I would dearly love to be proven wrong on that front 🤗\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI'm tempted to go 3.25* as I did like Lara more this time and the world expansion plus new characters were all fun but then I remember the OTT ending \u0026amp; Aren's (🤬) shenanigans and I cannot go higher than 3* ... this does, however give the series massive scope for improvement \u0026amp; based off the foreshadowed incoming MCs I hope it will 🤞","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3BRS6QLZZGI78\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.AZrVmBUlO9ey3o9t\"}}"},"likeCount":54,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":4},"User:82156089":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":82156089,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-asse